course: dictionary
lesson: 15707
title: Torn: ripped or undecided
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Torn comes from the verb tear, which means to rip or pull something apart. When something is torn, it has been ripped. A torn page has a rip in it, and a torn ticket has been pulled in two.
explain: «The page was torn, so Sam taped it back together.» The word was tells you that torn is working like a passive: something happened to the page. Check the meaning by swapping in ripped: the page was ripped, so Sam taped it back together. It still makes sense.
explain: Torn can also mean not able to choose. «He was torn between the red bike and the blue one.» He could not pick one, because he wanted both. Torn between two things means you are pulled in two directions in your mind.
explain: In maths, torn things can be taken away from the good ones. «A pack has 20 cards and 5 are torn.» Good cards = total − torn, so 20 − 5 = 15 good cards.
fact: Torn is the past participle of the verb tear: tear, tore, torn.
fact: «Torn» means ripped or pulled apart, so a torn page has a rip in it.
fact: «Torn between two things» means you cannot choose between them.
fact: In maths, good things = total − torn things.
fact: Words like torn can change their meaning with the words around them: a torn jumper is damaged, but a torn decision is a hard choice.
exercise: «The page was torn, so Sam taped it back together.» What does torn mean here? | *Ripped or pulled apart | Very wet | Clean and new | Folded neatly
exercise: A pack has 20 cards. 5 of the cards are torn. How many good cards are left? | 20 | 5 | 25 | *15
exercise: «He was torn between the red bike and the blue one.» What does torn between mean? | *Not able to choose | Riding both bikes at once | Pulled apart by two bikes | Very happy with both bikes
test: «Mia's jeans were torn at the knee.» What does torn mean in this sentence? | *Had a rip in them | Were too big | Were brand new | Were very dirty
test: The ticket was ___ in half. Which word fits the gap? | tearing | tear | *torn | tears
exam: «She was torn between staying and going.» What does this tell you about her? | *She could not decide what to do | She was running very fast | She had already left the room | She was ripping her clothes
